      "content": "The resistance in an AC circuit for a capacitor is determined by two factors: capacitance ($C$) and frequency ($f$). A larger capacitance or a higher frequency will result in lower capacitive reactance ($X_C$). For instance, if you double the frequency of an AC source while keeping the capacitor size the same, the capacitive reactance will be halved. This demonstrates that higher frequencies allow more current through the capacitor's charging/discharging action.",
